values ('ap_chemistry', 3, '3.1', array['3.1', '3.2']::text[], 'vocabulary', 'London dispersion forces', 'Coulombic interactions between temporary, fluctuating dipoles, often the strongest net intermolecular force between large molecules.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Do not use "London dispersion forces" as a synonym for "van der Waals forces."', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-chemistry-reference-u2-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_chemistry-u3-r1-001; ced=3.1.A.1 London dispersion forces are a result of the Coulombic interactions between temporary, fluctuating dipoles')
