values ('ap_chemistry', 3, '3.6', array['3.6']::text[], 'list_sequence', 'Causes of deviation from ideal gas behavior', 'Real gases can deviate from the ideal gas law for two reasons named in the CED.', '[{"label": "Interparticle attractions", "meaning": "Attractions among gas molecules, particularly at conditions close to those resulting in condensation."}, {"label": "Particle volumes", "meaning": "The volume of the particles themselves, particularly at extremely high pressures."}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-chemistry-reference-u2-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_chemistry-u3-r2-008; ced=3.6.A.1: "Deviations from the ideal gas law may result from interparticle attractions among gas molecules... Deviations may also arise from particle volumes"')
